{"id": "1.2-00032", "case_id": "opencores_aes_core_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/aes_core", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00032&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (5 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/verilog/aes_cipher_top.v, rtl/verilog/aes_inv_cipher_top.v, rtl/verilog/aes_inv_sbox.v, rtl/verilog/aes_key_expand_128.v, rtl/verilog/aes_rcon.v, rtl/verilog/aes_sbox.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00032&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>6 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00032&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Fverilog%2Faes_cipher_top.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>1 verification testpoints:</strong> bench/verilog/test_bench_top.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00032&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00032&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the AES Rijndael cipher and inverse-cipher project\n\nRead specification/project.txt and the unchanged original aes.pdf by Rudolf\nUsselmann, revision 1.1. Implement BOTH independent top interfaces aes_cipher_top\nand aes_inv_cipher_top and their shared key-expansion/S-box closure: six required\nfiles and six modules. This is one project with two public engines, as drawn in\nthe original architecture; no reference cipher engine is supplied during scoring.\naes_cipher_top is the primary build top, and the system bench instantiates both.\n\nCurator clarifications from the pinned RTL:\n- This release supports AES-128 only. All blocks/keys are 128 bits with the\n  standard AES byte ordering. aes_cipher_top accepts key and plaintext on a\n  rising clock with ld=1 and pulses done when text_out is the completed standard\n  AES ciphertext. Key expansion is started on every cipher ld. Do not overlap\n  encryption requests. Use done to observe completion; the manual describes a\n  twelve-clock sequence including load and output stage.\n- aes_inv_cipher_top first requires a rising-edge kld pulse with a stable key.\n  Allow twelve clocks for the forward round keys to be generated and stored in\n  reverse order, then pulse ld with the ciphertext. The input key need not remain\n  driven after its load edge. Subsequent decryptions may reuse the expanded key;\n  do not overlap key expansion and decryption. done pulses for the completed\n  plaintext. The manual lists an output kdone, but this pinned RTL does NOT expose\n  that port: it is internal and is not an externally usable handshake. Do not add\n  a kdone port to the required interface. Use the documented finite key-load wait.\n- rst is synchronous active LOW for both engines. Assert reset over several clk\n  rising edges, then release before operation. Reset initializes control counters;\n  idle/unloaded data registers are not all reset and their contents are unspecified.\n  Sample result data only with the corresponding done signal. The input must be\n  stable across the accepted rising edge; testbench drives change after that edge.\n- aes_key_expand_128 produces four 32-bit round-key words, most significant first.\n  kld loads the input key; subsequent clocks advance the standard AES-128 schedule\n  using RotWord, SubWord and Rcon. aes_rcon resets its sequence on kld to\n  0x01000000 and advances the AES round constant. aes_sbox/aes_inv_sbox are\n  combinational forward/inverse 8-bit AES substitutions. The cipher engines\n  implement the standard initial, iterative and final round transforms.\n- The supplied reference retains original #1 simulation annotations and the\n  harmless timescale.v include; these are not extra functionality to reproduce.\n  Generated RTL may be ordinary synthesizable RTL with the same clock behavior.\n  Only the fixed timescale.v support header may be included; no implementation\n  is provided through an include or through a golden companion engine.\n\nThe single original bench compares fixed ciphertext answers and decrypts each\nresult back to the known plaintext. It is one Boolean testpoint, not one point\nper vector. Implement both engines correctly; each engine has its own retained\ncompile-valid corruption control demonstrating detection in the shared bench.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/476fdc6eb48a6edcae8043cd8c78ed3657b385d2296e3ccc7a871a289a3ea2df.txt", "size": 14896, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/d9725a0e84faa2a51a01e870c3b021d841b0568926f0b0661e9c9216c8d540c8.txt", "size": 309, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/direct_adapter.json", "url": "assets/d59ebc0fc070d0518fe0475ec77f18ec9e010f9bc8b1ff3efb0d890cc4eaaf1d.txt", "size": 475, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/aes_cipher_top.v", "url": "assets/ab39a4a094dc8cfde90fcaa4c1aaf7dc9bf75b57ed762e11a985b88f6b23996c.txt", "size": 10139, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and 